msgid_plural "MarSec. T72s"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "MarSec. T72"
#. ~ Description of "MarSec. T72"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/7.50mm.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/7.50mm.json
msgid ""
"A massive, unwieldy revolver, using combined magnetic and chemical propulsion to fire 7.50mm rounds at energies that rival a sniping platform.  It additionally features a secondary barrel for a single 00 shot shell.\n"
"\n"
"The T72 remains a relic of the early hyperspace era, meant to be used by and against the posthuman.  Its perhaps most notable for its use by fictional rebel figures than for any sort of actual combat effectiveness."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of gun "landfall survival gun"
#. ~ Description of "landfall survival gun"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/7.50mm.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/7.50mm.json
msgid ""
"A lightweight, bolt-action gun that is barely more than a 7.50mm barrel "
"mounted within a flimsy metal assembly.  Cheaply made and outdated in all "
"respects, it's only useful in the most extenuating of circumstances."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
#. ~ Variant name of gun "G&W SR-P77"
#. ~ Variant name of item "G&W SR-P77"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/7.50mm.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/7.50mm.json
msgid "G&W SR-P77"
msgid_plural "G&W SR-P77s"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "G&W SR-P77"
#. ~ Description of variant "G&W SR-P77" of gun "G&W SR-P77"
#. ~ Description of "G&W SR-P77"
#. ~ Description of variant "G&W SR-P77" of item "G&W SR-P77"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/7.50mm.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/7.50mm.json
msgid ""
"Compact and powerful, the SR-77 serves as the current main firearm of UICA "
"assault teams, having replaced the SR-P9 in the very last decade of the "
"reclamation wars.  Designed for combat withing the tight confines of "
"spacecraft and habitats, the SR-77 is a bullpup carbine with a top-mounted "
"magazine and a high rate of fire.  Performance in open terrain is subpar."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "G&W SR-P77"
#. ~ Variant name of item "G&W SR-P77"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/7.50mm.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/7.50mm.json
msgid "Gibson-77 Sentinel"
msgid_plural "Gibson-77 Sentinels"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "G&W SR-P77" of gun "Gibson-77 Sentinel"
#. ~ Description of variant "Gibson-77 Sentinel" of item "G&W SR-P77"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/7.50mm.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/7.50mm.json
msgid ""
"A rare version of the m90-UASTA PDW built to its original private market "
"specifications, featuring an ergonomic bullpup design and a large magazine "
"capacity underneath a sleek white and chromed finish.  Actual combat "
"performance is slightly improved over the more common military model, due to "
"the use of higher-quality materials within the barrel and ETC ignition "
"system."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/7.50mm.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/7.50mm.json
msgid "Wraitheon Vahagn 10XR"
msgid_plural "Wraitheon Vahagn 10XRs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "Wraitheon Vahagn 10XR"
#. ~ Description of "Wraitheon Vahagn 10XR"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/7.50mm.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/7.50mm.json
msgid ""
"The legendary apex of smartgun technology, believed to be an urban legend by most.  Bleeding-edge targeting systems allow it to track up 10 distinct targets simultaneously, with every trigger pull delivering a burst of two 7.5mm microjet darts to each target with a precision that is best described as supernatural.  One needs only to point the weapon in the general direction of the enemy, and the Vahagn will do the rest.\n"
"\n"
"Prohibitive cost and complexity kept this weapon from ever seeing the light of day, and only a handful of prototypes are believed to exist within the black market.  Finding one here can only mean that corporate forces beyond the ordinary have made Salus IV their battleground."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Firing mode of gun
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/7.50mm.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/7.50mm.json
msgid "SMART TRACK"
msgstr ""

