msgid_plural "GG-860 Wasp Rifles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "GG-860 Wasp Rifle"
#. ~ Description of "GG-860 Wasp Rifle"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/needle.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/needle.json
msgid ""
"This light coilgun fires 3x35mm armor-piercing flechette.  Classified as a "
"support crew weapon that can be stashed in hidden lockers throughout the "
"floors of a ship.  Designed to be fired in short bursts, if the flechettes "
"pierce a ship's hull they leave tiny holes that are easily repaired."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/needle.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/needle.json
msgid "3x35mm automatic 'Wandering Priest' coilpistol"
msgid_plural "3x35mm automatic 'Wandering Priest' coilpistols"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "3x35mm automatic 'Wandering Priest' coilpistol"
#. ~ Description of "3x35mm automatic 'Wandering Priest' coilpistol"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/needle.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/needle.json
msgid ""
"An automatic coilgun made entirely of lightweight ceramics, with no moving "
"pieces and if loaded with splinter rounds almost entirely invisible on most "
"security scanners.  No one is sure who manufactures this assassin's tool, but"
" they randomly come onto the back room markets frequented by the unsavory."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/plasma.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/plasma.json
msgid "Magnadrive 230K"
msgid_plural "Magnadrive 230K"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "Magnadrive 230K"
#. ~ Description of "Magnadrive 230K"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/plasma.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/plasma.json
msgid ""
"A heavy plasma railgun that easily defeats most forms of conventional armor "
"and flash-incinerates anything  behind it.  Its large size and liability to "
"overheat make it unsuitable for infantry use, but it is a common sight on "
"military vehicles and in the hands of power-armored troops, especially when "
"heavy armor is expected."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
